@startuml
' Figure 1.1 -- The agent skeleton.
' A state machine whose transitions are driven by model output. Executing a
' tool is the only state that reaches anything outside the process; every
' other transition is bookkeeping the loop does to itself.

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam state {
  BorderThickness 1
}

[*] --> Deciding : task arrives

state "Deciding\nask the model what to do next" as Deciding
state "Executing a tool\nthe only state that reaches outside" as Executing
state "Verifying\nrun the checks" as Verifying

Deciding --> Executing : model emits\na tool call
Executing --> Deciding : result appended\nto state
Deciding --> Verifying : model signals\ncompletion
Verifying --> Deciding : checks failed
Verifying --> [*] : checks passed

note right of Executing
  Files, network, compiler,
  anything outside the process.
  No other state can reach them.
end note

note left of Deciding
  State carried across
  transitions: the task,
  what has been tried,
  what came back.
end note

@enduml
